IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clca-dates`
IMPORT `clca-child-abuse`

-- Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002 (ACT), chapter 8A, with Limitation Act 1985 s 21C -- worked cases for the questions of the
-- person abused as a child.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the date` d m y

`ANY DAY` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

§ `s 114A, s 114AA -- is my claim a child abuse claim`

`CAC YES` MEANS `yes: a child abuse claim (s 114A, s 114AA)`
`CAC NO` MEANS `no: a child abuse claim is a claim for personal injury arising from physical or sexual abuse suffered as a child (the text's no, s 114A, s 114AA (1))`
`CAC JUSTIFIED` MEANS `no: physical abuse does not include conduct justified or excused under a law applying in the ACT (the text's no, s 114AA (2))`
`CAC OPEN` MEANS `sexual abuse includes offences and misconduct of a sexual nature, and the list is not closed; whether this counts is not said (NOTHING-kind, s 114AA (2))`

#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `physical abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC YES`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `physical abuse` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC JUSTIFIED`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC YES`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `misconduct of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC YES`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `other sexual abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC OPEN`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `something that was neither physical nor sexual abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC NO`
-- Not a personal injury claim; abuse after turning 18; injury not arising from the abuse.
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` FALSE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CAC NO`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `CAC NO`
#ASSERT `s 114A -- is my claim a child abuse claim` TRUE `physical abuse` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CAC NO`

§ `Limitation Act 1985 s 21C -- is there a time limit`

`NO LIMIT` MEANS `no time limit: the action may be brought at any time and no limitation period applies (Limitation Act 1985 s 21C (2)); the court may still stay a proceeding that can no longer be tried fairly (s 21C (3))`
`ORDINARY LIMITS` MEANS `s 21C does not apply: the ordinary limitation periods of the Limitation Act 1985 apply (the text's no, s 21C (1))`

#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO LIMIT`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `physical abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO LIMIT`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `misconduct of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO LIMIT`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `physical abuse` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `other sexual abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `something that was neither physical nor sexual abuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` TRUE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`
#ASSERT `Limitation Act s 21C -- is there a time limit on my claim` FALSE `an offence of a sexual nature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ORDINARY LIMITS`

§ `s 114BB, s 114BBA -- was the organisation responsible for me`

`RESP CARE` MEANS `yes: it exercised care, supervision or authority over you (s 114BBA (1))`
`RESP DELEGATED` MEANS `yes: it delegated care, supervision or authority over you to another organisation, so each is responsible (s 114BBA (2))`
`NOT RESP` MEANS `no: it neither exercised nor delegated care, supervision or authority over you (the text's no, s 114BBA)`

#ASSERT `s 114BBA -- is the organisation responsible for me` `an ACT administrative unit (a government directorate)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `RESP CARE`
#ASSERT `s 114BBA -- is the organisation responsible for me` `a territory authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `RESP CARE`
#ASSERT `s 114BBA -- is the organisation responsible for me` `an unincorporated body (such as a club, association or church body that is not incorporated)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RESP DELEGATED`
#ASSERT `s 114BBA -- is the organisation responsible for me` `another organisation (such as a company, incorporated association, school or religious body)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT RESP`
#ASSERT `s 114BBA -- is the organisation responsible for me` `an individual, not an organisation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `part 8A.1A speaks of organisations; it does not say whether an individual is one (NOTHING-kind, s 114BB)`

§ `s 114BBC -- was the abuser associated with the organisation`

`ASSOC OPEN` MEANS `s 114BBC lists who is associated without closing the list; it does not say whether this person is (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 114BBC -- is the abuser associated with the organisation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an office holder, officer, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the organisation (s 114BBC (1) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 114BBC -- is the abuser associated with the organisation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a religious leader or other member of the personnel of a religious organisation (s 114BBC (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 114BBC -- is the abuser associated with the organisation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: associated with the organisation it delegated responsibility for you to (s 114BBC (3))`
-- "Personnel" of an organisation that is not religious, and a religious organisation's non-personnel: outside the list.
#ASSERT `s 114BBC -- is the abuser associated with the organisation` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ASSOC OPEN`
#ASSERT `s 114BBC -- is the abuser associated with the organisation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ASSOC OPEN`

§ `s 114BC -- was the abuser an employee, or akin to one`

`EMP OPEN` MEANS `s 114BC does not say whether this person counts as an employee (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 114BC -- is the abuser an employee of the organisation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an employee of the organisation (s 114BC (1))`
#ASSERT `s 114BC -- is the abuser an employee of the organisation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: akin to an employee, carrying out activities that are part of its ordinary activities and for its benefit (s 114BC (2) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 114BC -- is the abuser an employee of the organisation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EMP OPEN`
#ASSERT `s 114BC -- is the abuser an employee of the organisation` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `EMP OPEN`

§ `ss 114BBB, 114BBD, 114BE -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable`

`BOTH ROUTES` MEANS `both: it is taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse (s 114BBD (3)), and it is vicariously liable for its employee's abuse (s 114BE (1))`
`DUTY ROUTE` MEANS `the duty route: it is taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse unless it proves it took reasonable precautions, and here it has not (s 114BBD (3))`
`VICARIOUS ROUTE` MEANS `the vicarious route: it is vicariously liable for its employee's abuse, whenever it happened (s 114BE (1), s 114BA)`
`NEITHER ROUTE` MEANS `neither statutory route holds on these facts; the common law of negligence and vicarious liability still applies (NOTHING-kind, s 114BE (3))`

-- The commencement edge: 16 May 2026 is in, 15 May 2026 is out (s 114BBB; division 8A.1A.2 commenced 16 May 2026).
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 16 5 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `BOTH ROUTES`
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 15 5 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `VICARIOUS ROUTE`
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 16 5 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DUTY ROUTE`
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 15 5 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`
-- 13 November 2025 (the day part 8A.1A commenced, and the date the earlier baseline uses for the duty): the duty does
-- not reach it, because division 8A.1A.2 came later (finding 1).
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 13 11 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`
-- The organisation proves reasonable precautions: only the vicarious route is left, if it holds.
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `VICARIOUS ROUTE`
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`
-- Abuse long ago: vicarious liability reaches it (s 114BA).
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 3 1990) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `VICARIOUS ROUTE`
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 3 1990) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`
-- Not responsible for the child: neither route.
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`
-- Abuse not in connection with the organisation's responsibility: no reversed onus.
#ASSERT `ch 8A -- on what grounds can I hold the organisation liable` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NEITHER ROUTE`

§ `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust`

`RELATED` MEANS `yes: a related trust of the body: it controls the trust and uses it to conduct its activities (s 114B)`
`NOT CONTROLLED` MEANS `no: the body does not control the trust in any of the ways s 114B (2) lists (the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RELATED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT CONTROLLED`
#ASSERT `s 114B -- is the trust a related trust of the body` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the body does not use the trust to conduct its activities (the text's no, s 114B (1))`

§ `s 114F -- whom do I sue for the unincorporated body`

#ASSERT `s 114F -- whom do I sue for the unincorporated body` TRUE `not yet` EQUALS `the body itself, in its own name: you may start or continue the proceeding before a defendant is nominated or appointed, and the court may make interlocutory orders against the body as if it were incorporated (s 114F (1), (2))`
#ASSERT `s 114F -- whom do I sue for the unincorporated body` TRUE `the body nominated a defendant` EQUALS `the nominee: your claim may be brought against the entity the body nominated, which is the defendant for the body for all purposes and can be found liable for what the body would owe if incorporated (s 114D (4)); orders already made against the body still bind it (s 114F (3))`
#ASSERT `s 114F -- whom do I sue for the unincorporated body` TRUE `the court appointed a related trust as defendant` EQUALS `the appointed trust: your claim may be brought or continued against the related trust the court appointed, which is the defendant for the body for all purposes and can be found liable for what the body would owe if incorporated (s 114E (5)); orders already made against the body still bind it (s 114F (3))`
#ASSERT `s 114F -- whom do I sue for the unincorporated body` FALSE `not yet` EQUALS `part 8A.2 deals only with child abuse claims against unincorporated bodies; it says nothing here (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 114E (3) -- the body's 28 days to tell the court about its related trusts`

-- 1 March 2027 + 28 days = 29 March 2027; 15 February 2028 + 28 days = 14 March 2028 (2028 is a leap year: 14 days to
-- 29 February, 14 more into March); 20 December 2026 + 28 days = 17 January 2027 (across the year end).
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- the last day for the body to tell the court about its related trusts` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `on` 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- the last day for the body to tell the court about its related trusts` (`on` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `on` 14 3 2028
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- the last day for the body to tell the court about its related trusts` (`on` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `on` 17 1 2027

`TOLD IN TIME` MEANS `yes: the body told the court about its related trusts within 28 days of your application (s 114E (3))`
`TOLD LATE` MEANS `no: the body did not tell the court about its related trusts within 28 days of your application, in breach of s 114E (3); the court may still appoint a related trust it was not told about (s 114E (4))`
`STILL TIME` MEANS `not yet due: the body has not told the court yet, and its 28 days have not ended (s 114E (3))`

-- Told on the last day, the day after, the day after the application.
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`on` 29 3 2027) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `TOLD IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`on` 30 3 2027) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `TOLD LATE`
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`on` 2 3 2027) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `TOLD IN TIME`
-- Not told: today is the last day, the day after, the day of the application.
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `STILL TIME`
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `TOLD LATE`
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `STILL TIME`
-- Leap-year application: told on 14 March 2028 is in time, 15 March late.
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 15 2 2028) TRUE (`on` 14 3 2028) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `TOLD IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 114E (3) -- has the body told the court in time` (`on` 15 2 2028) TRUE (`on` 15 3 2028) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `TOLD LATE`

§ `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee`

-- Liability $350,000 against trust property of $400,000, exactly $350,000, and $1 over it; settlement and costs above
-- trust property of $150,000; nothing owed.
#ASSERT `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee` 300000 0 50000 400000 EQUALS 350000
#ASSERT `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee` 300000 0 50000 350000 EQUALS 350000
#ASSERT `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee` 300000 0 50001 350000 EQUALS 350000
#ASSERT `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee` 0 200000 20000 150000 EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `s 114G -- the most I can recover from the trustee` 0 0 0 1000 EQUALS 0

§ `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement`

`ASA (i)` MEANS `yes: made before 26 August 2016, when the limitation period for your claim had already ended (s 114J (1) (b) (i))`
`ASA (ii)` MEANS `yes: made before 10 December 2022, and not just and reasonable in the circumstances (s 114J (1) (b) (ii))`
`ASA (iii)` MEANS `yes: made before 13 November 2025, and the abuser would have been an employee of an organisation under part 8A.1A (s 114J (1) (b) (iii))`
`NOT ASA (a)` MEANS `no: it does not settle a child abuse claim and bar a claim to which Limitation Act s 21C applies (the text's no, s 114J (1) (a))`
`NOT ASA (b)` MEANS `no: none of the three kinds of past settlement in s 114J (1) (b) (the text's no)`

-- (i): the day before s 21C commenced, and the day it commenced.
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 25 8 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ASA (i)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 26 8 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ASA (b)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 25 8 2016) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ASA (b)`
-- (ii): the day before part 8A.3 commenced, and the day it commenced.
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 26 8 2016) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ASA (ii)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 9 12 2022) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ASA (ii)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 10 12 2022) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ASA (b)`
-- (iii): the day before part 8A.1A commenced, and the day it commenced.
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 10 12 2022) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ASA (iii)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 12 11 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ASA (iii)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 13 11 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT ASA (b)`
-- All three limbs hold: the first is named (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ASA (i)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ASA (b)`
-- Limb (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT ASA (a)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT ASA (a)`
#ASSERT `s 114J -- is my settlement an abuse settlement agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT ASA (a)`

§ `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside`

`SET ASIDE (a)` MEANS `yes, it can be: you may sue and apply to set it aside (s 114K (2)), and the court may set it aside because there were legal barriers to full compensation when it was made (s 114K (3) (a))`
`SET ASIDE (b)` MEANS `yes, it can be: you may sue and apply to set it aside (s 114K (2)), and the court may set it aside because it is not just and reasonable now (s 114K (3) (b))`
`APPLY ONLY` MEANS `you may sue and apply (s 114K (2)), but the court may set it aside only if satisfied of legal barriers then or that it is not just and reasonable now, and on these facts it is not (the text's no, s 114K (3))`
`NOT PART 8A.3` MEANS `no: part 8A.3 applies only to an abuse settlement agreement, and this is not one (the text's no, s 114K (1), s 114J)`

#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SET ASIDE (a)`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `APPLY ONLY`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2018) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SET ASIDE (b)`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2018) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SET ASIDE (a)`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2024) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `APPLY ONLY`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SET ASIDE (b)`
-- Made after 13 November 2025, or not a settlement of a child abuse claim: part 8A.3 does not reach it.
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 2 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT PART 8A.3`
#ASSERT `s 114K -- can my settlement be set aside` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 7 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT PART 8A.3`

§ `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this`

`MUST NOT -- NOT SET ASIDE FIRST` MEANS `no: the court may set aside other things only if it decides to set aside the settlement itself (the text's no, s 114L (1))`

#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `a contract, deed or other agreement that gives effect to the settlement` EQUALS `yes, it may be: the court may also set aside a contract, deed or other agreement that gives effect to the settlement (s 114L (1) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `an order or judgment of a court that gives effect to the settlement` EQUALS `yes, it may be: the court may also set aside an order or judgment of a court that gives effect to the settlement (s 114L (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `a deed of release I signed accepting a National Redress Scheme offer, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in that offer` EQUALS `no: the court must not set aside a National Redress Scheme deed of release or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in the offer (the text's no, s 114L (2) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `an agreement, so far as it settled a cross-claim between defendants or one defendant indemnified another` EQUALS `no: the court must not set aside an agreement so far as it settled a cross-claim between defendants or one defendant indemnified another (the text's no, s 114L (2) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `a contract of insurance` EQUALS `no: the court must not set aside a contract of insurance (the text's no, s 114L (2) (c))`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` TRUE `something that does not give effect to the settlement` EQUALS `s 114L reaches only things that give effect to the settlement; it says nothing about this (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` FALSE `a contract, deed or other agreement that gives effect to the settlement` EQUALS `MUST NOT -- NOT SET ASIDE FIRST`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` FALSE `an order or judgment of a court that gives effect to the settlement` EQUALS `MUST NOT -- NOT SET ASIDE FIRST`
#ASSERT `s 114L -- can the court also set aside this` FALSE `a contract of insurance` EQUALS `no: the court must not set aside a contract of insurance (the text's no, s 114L (2) (c))`

§ `s 114M -- must I pay back what I received`

#ASSERT `s 114M -- must I pay back what I received` TRUE EQUALS `no: what you were paid under the settlement (including legal costs or disbursements) is not recoverable from you, though the court may take it into account in deciding your damages; the settlement is void only so far as it relates to you (s 114M)`
#ASSERT `s 114M -- must I pay back what I received` FALSE EQUALS `s 114M speaks only of a settlement the court has set aside; until then the settlement stands (NOTHING-kind)`
